# Keys that vouch for packages (OpenSSH "allowed signers" format). `packages.py` checks the signature of a package
# zip against the lines of this file and of docs/ai/local/package-signers with `ssh-keygen -Y verify -I
# act-packages -n act-package`; a package no key line of either file vouches for is not verified, and
# `packages-unverified` in docs/ai/config.md decides whether one is admitted.
#
# One key per line, no comment on the same line:
#   act-packages namespaces="act-package" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
# The identity must read `act-packages`; `namespaces="act-package"` keeps the key from vouching for anything else.
# A public key is made with `ssh-keygen -t ed25519`; the public half (the `.pub` file, one line starting with
# `ssh-ed25519`) is what goes behind the first two words. Never put a private key here.
#
# The template ships one key: that of the template author, who signs the template's own packages. A project trusts
# a signer of its own in docs/ai/local/package-signers and leaves this file as it is (`R-work-override`).
act-packages namespaces="act-package" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIH7+DcHaTDX7t3RTrDVgEZIMJvtFcsx198cZZTXVhsab
